values ('e7f8a9b0-1c2d-4e27-8a67-7b8c9d0e1f27', 'introduction-to-theater', 'Introduction to Theater', 'Introduction to Theater is a first-year survey of theatrical art, history, and practice. The course introduces students to theater as a live collaborative event, a literary and performance tradition, a technical and design practice, and a public conversation shaped by artists and audiences. Students should leave able to watch theater more intelligently, read plays as performance, recognize major roles and traditions, understand the labor behind the event, and write about performance with evidence and care.');

